 "halflife": 40000,
 "note": "E-056b: the SAME token-substrate configuration at K=144 - does the dense two-year slab hold up on tokens, and what does it cost? Runs on an 80 GB H100 because #495 measured that K=144 at batch 256 does NOT fit a 24 GB 4090, while its control #478 ran that batch on a bigger card - halving the batch would confound K with batch, so the CARD is what changes. Keeps znoise 0.7 deliberately: it shares #504's dose exactly, so K=24 vs K=144 WITHIN tokens is a clean within-dose contrast even though the pre-registered token-scale confound makes the token-vs-d_z-32 LEVEL uninterpretable at that dose. Control #478 0.0820. LR schedule verified against #504's own stage2_lr records.",
 "published_at": "2026-08-28T08:40:51.793Z"
}
